.TH TUXTOYS-SETTINGS 1 2026-10-09 "TuxToys" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tuxtoys-settings \- set up TuxToys' tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuxtoys-settings
.RB [ \-\-page
.IR TOOL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tuxtoys-settings
opens the TuxToys window. Its first page, Home, lists every tool with a switch to turn
it on or off. The General page beside it shows the version, switches the panel icon on or
off, and backs up every tool's settings to a file, or restores them from one. Each tool
also has a page of its own in the sidebar, where it is set up.
Escape closes the window, and starting it again brings the open window to the front.
.PP
The settings are kept by the TuxToys service of the session, which starts on its own if
it is not running yet.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " TOOL"
Shows a tool's page, by the tool's module name, such as
.BR textextractor ,
as
.B tuxtoys modules
lists them; in the window already open, if there is one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tuxtoys/config.json
The settings, one section per module.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/tuxtoys/settings-window.ini
Whether the window has greeted you on its first open.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tuxtoys (1)
